/**
\mainpage

![MITK Logo][logo]

The [Medical Imaging Interaction Toolkit][mitk] (MITK) is a free, open-source
framework for medical image computing, developed at the [German Cancer Research
Center (DKFZ)][dkfz]. You can use it in two ways:

<ul>
<li><b>As an application.</b> The MITK Workbench is a ready-to-run program for
visualization, segmentation, and registration of CT, MRI, PET, and other DICOM
data.
<li><b>As a framework.</b> The MITK C++ libraries and plugin system let you extend
the Workbench or build your own medical imaging software.
</ul>

MITK combines [ITK][itk] and [VTK][vtk] with data management, advanced
visualization, and interaction in a single, modular framework.

<h2>Getting started</h2>

<ul>
<li><b>Use the Workbench.</b> The \ref UserManualPortal covers common tasks such as
loading, saving, and navigating data; see \ref PluginListPage for the individual
tools.
<li><b>Automate with the command-line apps.</b> The \ref MITKCmdAppsPage lists the
tools that ship with the Workbench for file conversion, segmentation, registration,
and model fitting in scripts and batch pipelines.
<li><b>Develop with MITK.</b> Start with the \ref BuildInstructionsPage, then read
\ref StartingDevelopment and the \ref HowToNewProject guide. Browse the
<a href="@MITK_DOXYGEN_GROUPS_PAGE@">API reference</a> and consult the
\ref CMAKE_FAQ while setting up your project.
</ul>

<h2>License</h2>

MITK is released under a [BSD-style license][license], free for both research and
commercial use. It is not a certified medical product and must not be used in
patient care.

<h2>Links</h2>

 - [Homepage][mitk]
 - [Download][download]
 - [Source code on GitHub][github]

